==English==

===Etymology===
An otherwise obsolete use of {{m|en|me}} in a dative context without a preposition (such as {{m|en|at}} or {{m|en|on}}).

Compare the identical {{cog|de|[[Weh]] [[ist]] [[mir]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˌwəʊ ɪz ˈmiː/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌwoʊ ɪz ˈmi/}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|sometimes|humorous}} {{ngd|Used to show that the speaker feels [[distress]] or [[misery]].}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|3|1|passage=Blasted with extasie. Oh, '''woe is me''',<br>T'haue seene what I haue seene: see what I see.|page=266|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/mrvvilliamshakes00shak/page/266/mode/1up|column=1}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalms|120|5||'''Woe is me''', that I soiourne in Mesech: that I dwell in the tents of Kedar.}}

